\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-270\li405\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0   The men of God cry out, bear witness;
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0\qj The watchmen who on lion's rampant stand,
\par Who day and night are never silent,
\par With confidence the enemy withstand.
\par This trumpet sound thro'out the whole world rings,
\par And multitudes from every nation brings.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li405\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.   Oh, that this fire brightly burning!
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0\qj Oh, that it would to ev'ry country spread!
\par    O Lord, that more might have the yearning
\par To help Thy cause and labour in Thy stead!
\par   O Lord, from high the earthly harvest view;
\par The harvest's great, but labourers so few!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li405\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.    Thy son has shown us very clearly,
\par \pard\li405\sl180\slmult0\qj What we should ask of Thee, O God of love.
\par  O see, how ev'rywhere sincerely,
\par Thy children's hearts are turned to things above!
\par They are united in one earnest plea;
\par To hear Thee say, dear Lord: "So shall it be."
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li405\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.   Thy work proceeds as was intended,
\par \pard\li405\sl180\slmult0\qj   For judgment and deliverance are Thine!
\par Then mankind's suffering will be ended
\par Tho' now Thy children under burdens pine!
\par Faith never ceases pleading, Lord, to Thee,
\par For Thy response will far exceed our plea!
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

